{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411679-what-exactly-do-celestial-gods-do-daily","id":1411679,"title":"What exactly do Celestial Gods *do* daily?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-03T12:54:05-07:00","id":1411679,"title":"What exactly do Celestial Gods *do* daily?","content":"Basically every single bit of info on the matter shows that gods are not total masters of their domains and they mostly happen on their own. The Sun and the Moon are not literally directed by their respective Incarnae, for instance, and likewise, the pattern spiders mostly &quot;run&quot; Exalted's closest equivalent of physical laws. There is no god of falling making sure that things fall. Artificial flying machines are not dependent on Vanileth's grace and existence. Exaltation happens irrespective of Lytek.<br /> <br /> But there's also contradicting information. For instance, apparently all weather happens thanks to the weather gods--that is, it only snows in the winter because the snow/blizzard/hail/etc. gods <i>make</i> it snow (and if you go off 2e it was actually the FA Solars that drafted the weather patterns which is...well, that's <i>very 2e</i> to put it nicely). Likewise, all battles not featuring essence users apparently are controlled by the Crimson Panoply of Victory? The books imply that they are the ultimate deciders of who wins any conflict in Creation, and aren't merely, say, recorders of the battles or shepherds over them making sure they go smoothly--no, the war gods actually like get together and actively decide everything that happens and who wins. The only exception is when essence wielders get involved.<br /> <br /> So outside of fate planning gods and the like, what do the vast majority of gods in Yu-Shan <i>actually do</i>? It appears that the overwhelmingly majority are not explicit controllers of things in Creation, they just...file paperwork and get into petty shitflinging politcking with others. Do most Celestials really just sit on their asses? I guess that's kind of the point, but it feels a bit odd that gods of concepts have no real control over these concepts and just officially hold these titles. I may just be reading the books wrong, but Yu-Shan's 2e book in particular implies that the vast majority of Celestials are desk jockeys that spend more time starting shit than actually doing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T13:48:01-07:00","id":1411689,"title":"","content":"The way I've viewed it is that in most cases a god's job is generally observational with the potential for manipulation when needed. This is for scenarios where everything is running properly and discounting corruption and all that. So normally what would happen would be the god observes the river flow or the rain season and details what happens and how it all proceeded. This would be to enable informing other parts of the process so they could properly prepare or make sure things are going with accordance to how they're supposed to operate. Ie Weather Bureau would notify of how much rain an area got so the local river gods would know whether to expect or more or less flooding than usual and so on and so forth. <br /> <br /> Then we have when stuff goes wrong because a group of elementals/demons/exalts/etc did something you now have way more rain going on and the plans now need to be adjusted for the fact that the plans around the area only account for the flooding resultant from 3 inches of rain that month and they're about to get the flooding from 1 foot of rain in the last week. Part of this would be to potentially warn off and prepare things to accommodate the overflow and limit damage there of to acceptable reasons. Then you would have the Weather Bureau adjusting the weather patterns so that the area doesn't suffer more damage because the original did not account for what just happened. So the gods would be ensuring less rain for a while and possibly warmer weather to avoid further flooding to the zone.<br /> <br /> Then there might be things like interaction with Mortals who will have their own wants. Potentially this would be things like arbitrating out an arrangement so a local mortal population can fish, or have lumber for fire and housing without destroying the entire forest that is home to a number of beasts and spirit types, while not getting the entire mortal population exterminated several of the smaller forest gods, residents, and spirits don't want the mortals messing with their forests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T15:17:25-07:00","id":1411708,"title":"","content":"I think Third Edition will do some things differently. Until it gets more focus, the questions can only be addressed in terms of prior Editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411679-what-exactly-do-celestial-gods-do-daily#post1411679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's also contradicting information. For instance, apparently all weather happens thanks to the weather gods--that is, it only snows in the winter because the snow/blizzard/hail/etc. gods <i>make</i> it snow (and if you go off 2e it was actually the FA Solars that drafted the weather patterns which is...well, that's <i>very 2e</i> to put it nicely).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think of this in terms of climate needing to be micromanaged in a world where we kind of have to assume things like heat and fluid dynamics work recognisably, but we want things to resemble Earth's biomes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, all battles not featuring essence users apparently are controlled by the Crimson Panoply of Victory? The books imply that they are the ultimate deciders of who wins any conflict in Creation, and aren't merely, say, recorders of the battles or shepherds over them making sure they go smoothly--no, the war gods actually like get together and actively decide everything that happens and who wins. The only exception is when essence wielders get involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be taking this further than it is depicted in the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that's kind of the point, but it feels a bit odd that gods of concepts have no real control over these concepts and just officially hold these titles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a bit overstating it when they can still control things when they elect to intervene, it's just that things will work themselves out naturally without constant fine tuning.<br /> <br /> But yes, in prior Editions the background mythology of the setting is more or less that the gods overthrew the Primordials to free themselves of constant labour and thereafter, apart from the existentially necessary work of Destiny and Seasons, divine life becomes one that largely consists of collecting data on matters of the world's functions (much of which can then be consulted by Destiny and Seasons to help them do their jobs properly), ceremonial administrative duties and generally residing in splendour. I think there's a degree to which gods may provide interventions in accordance with their own intentions and response to mortal prayers, pending the proper approval.<br /> <br /> I find this effectively draws on several forms of real life mythology and certain forms of government, while also fulfilling the pulp revival intentions and cynical edge of the original writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T16:59:49-07:00","id":1411720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411679-what-exactly-do-celestial-gods-do-daily#post1411679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So outside of fate planning gods and the like, what do the vast majority of gods in Yu-Shan actually do?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Rp7jp5H-xWU\" data-code=\"Rp7jp5H-xWU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Rp7jp5H-xWU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T18:10:17-07:00","id":1411725,"title":"","content":"Gods of the celestial bureacracy oversee Creation like gardeners oversee an outdoor greenhouse with a retractable roof. Mostly things just go on by themselves, bugs come, they go, the plants grow. If a bunch of bad bugs come you might need to step in and use your awesome powers to fix the problem. You also might find that some of your gardeners are pilfering berries, and you might want to stop that. Also some of the plants, but only some of them, can petition you to do things for them.<br /> <br /> So you can, if you want to, make it rain by turning on the sprinklers, or make it stop raining by closing the roof, or turn on the lights, or close the shutters, forcibly move plants around, whatever. You don't have to do any of those things and the garden runs pretty fine without it, you may discuss with your fellow gardeners what to do about different situations, but generally you just let the garden go and party.<br /> <br /> That's basically gods, as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T11:30:26-07:00","id":1411842,"title":"","content":"I was expecting the first response to be \u2018hookers and blow\u2019.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T11:41:57-07:00","id":1411844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411679-what-exactly-do-celestial-gods-do-daily?p=1411725#post1411725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods of the celestial bureacracy oversee Creation like gardeners oversee an outdoor greenhouse with a retractable roof. Mostly things just go on by themselves, bugs come, they go, the plants grow. If a bunch of bad bugs come you might need to step in and use your awesome powers to fix the problem. You also might find that some of your gardeners are pilfering berries, and you might want to stop that. Also some of the plants, but only some of them, can petition you to do things for them.<br /> <br /> So you can, if you want to, make it rain by turning on the sprinklers, or make it stop raining by closing the roof, or turn on the lights, or close the shutters, forcibly move plants around, whatever. You don't have to do any of those things and the garden runs pretty fine without it, you may discuss with your fellow gardeners what to do about different situations, but generally you just let the garden go and party.<br /> <br /> That's basically gods, as far as I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never thought of it that way, the analogy is awesome. Thanks !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:45:19-07:00","id":1411857,"title":"","content":"As far as day to day life in Yu-Shan goes its worth noting that making Quintessence or Ambrosia into whatever you want is a specialised skill. So while everyone has the raw materials not everyone is equally capable of using them so keeping the gods at the level of luxury they have come to expect is an entire industry, to say nothing of Yu-Shans other inhabitants some of whom have direct physical needs. <br /> <br /> In my portrayals of Yu-Shan I double down on it being the capital of Creation under the Primordials and that the gods do not understand their new home as well as they would like. This also increases the need for services that exist for the sake of Yu-Shan being its own place with its own problems rather than everything being meaningless or needing to have a knock on effect in Creation.<br /> <br /> Also there is football, but that is a story for another time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T20:27:02-07:00","id":1411996,"title":"","content":"The Games of Divinity are fantasy football confirmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}